"""An unofficial client for the MAX messenger: large type, no web browser.

PyMax (MIT, vendored in /usr/local/lib/b8k-max) speaks MAX's web protocol
over a WebSocket, as web.max.ru does, so no web engine is loaded: about
55 MB in all instead of a second browser. The first start shows a QR code
to scan in MAX on a phone; the session is then kept in
~/.local/share/b8k-max/web.db (mode 600). PyMax's simulated telemetry is
off: a person is typing here.

Telemetry of our own instead, as MAX's app reports it, so that the server
sees an ordinary client and is less likely to block the account: the
screens a person really goes through (to the list, into a chat, the
window hidden) and how long a chat took to show, in the event shapes of
PyMax 2.4.1. No texts, no names. It is on until switched off in the
settings (the gear in the header), kept in ~/.config/b8k/max.conf with
the buzz on new messages.

Pages: the chat list (initials, name, last message, time, unread count)
and a chat (bubbles, photos, a large entry and a send button). New
messages arrive live and buzz (unless switched off in the settings).
The search (the magnifier over the list) finds a person by phone number,
to write to or add to the contacts, a channel or group by its max.ru link,
to join, or one of the own chats by name; a chat is deleted (a dialog, for
this account only) or left (a group, a channel) with the bin in its header,
after a question on the page. One thing at a time, by hand: nothing here
searches or adds in bulk.

MAX has no setting for who may write to an account, so by default the
dialogs of people outside the contacts are kept off the list, the badge
and the buzz here (the settings switch them back). Known are the contacts
MAX sends at login, those added here, those written to here, and, the
first time, everyone already in a dialog; the ids are kept in
~/.local/share/b8k-max/known.json (mode 600), since after the first login
MAX sends only the contacts that changed. Who may add the account to chats
is a setting of MAX itself; contacts only by default, sent once per account
(and when switched), not at every login, so a change on the phone stays.
PyMax runs in its own thread with an asyncio loop; every call from the
window goes through run(), every answer comes back with GLib.idle_add.

It lives in the background: b8k-launcher starts it with --background at
session start, closing the window only hides it, and the panel's MAX
button brings the same process back (one instance through D-Bus). The
unread count of dialogs and groups (channels left out) goes to
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/b8k-badge/max, which b8k-launch shows on the button, and
the panel is told at once (b8k_ui.badge, with the button's own signal). Chats open from a cache: the last
messages of each chat on disk (~/.cache/b8k-max/chats, mode 600) and the
last six chats kept built in memory; a chat with nothing new since its
cache opens without asking MAX at all. The list keeps its rows and redraws
only a chat that changed. Photos are cached on disk and pruned when not
shown for a month (daily, as the program runs for weeks).

The list has two tabs, chats and channels. A long press on a chat pins it
to the top or switches its notifications (buzz and the panel's count);
channels are quiet unless switched on. Both are kept here
(~/.local/share/b8k-max/chats.json): PyMax has no pinning or muting.

A chat opens with its cache and the newest PAGE messages; two older pages
follow in the background, the rest as the reader scrolls up, keeping the
place. A chat left keeps only its newest BUBBLES built, and photos are
fetched only near the screen. Voice messages play in the bubble (libmpv,
sound only); a video opens full screen in b8k-vplay (mpv elsewhere) and a
file in the browser, by the short-lived link MAX gives on request.

Reactions: a long press on a message offers six emoji; those on it show
under it with their counts, the own one highlighted, a tap puts one on or
takes the own off. Others' reactions arrive live.

The person of a dialog can be renamed (the pencil): here only, kept in
~/.local/share/b8k-max/names.json, since MAX's web protocol as PyMax has it
offers no renaming of contacts.
"""
